 ## Overview
-2D Mask Matching aligns 2D instance masks predicted from different camera views to a consistent set of 3D instances detected by a NeRF-based detector (specifically NeRF-RCNN) [S1]. It solves the problem of inconsistent instance labeling across views, where the same physical object might receive different instance IDs or be missed entirely in different images [S1]. Unlike standard per-pixel losses, this method establishes a one-to-one correspondence between predicted 2D masks and 3D instances using Intersection over Union (IoU), ensuring multi-view consistency for the instance field [S1, S2].
+2D Mask Matching aligns 2D instance masks predicted from different camera views to a consistent set of 3D instances detected by a NeRF-based detector (specifically NeRF-RCNN) [S1]. It solves the problem of inconsistent instance labeling across views, where the same physical object might receive different instance IDs or be missed entirely in different images [S1]. Unlike standard per-pixel losses, this method establishes a one-to-one correspondence between predicted 2D masks and 3D instances using Intersection over Union (IoU), ensuring multi-view consistency for the instance field [S1].
 
